From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gautham Chettiar <gauthamchettiar@email.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 08:27:27 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Don't depend on reqwest when targeting WebAssembly

reqwest's blocking client needs tokio's networking and a native TLS stack,
neither of which builds for wasm32 targets. Make it a native-only dependency
of link_checker and templates:

- link_checker: external links can't be checked on wasm; check_url returns
  an error saying so. StatusCode now comes from the `http` crate, which
  reqwest re-exports, so the public type is unchanged.
- load_data: loading a remote URL errors on wasm, or returns none when
  `required=false`, matching how a failed optional fetch behaves natively.
  Request arguments are still validated.

Native builds are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
